# Time Complexity Analysis

## Project Overview

The Student Study & Assignment Planner uses an ArrayList
to store assignment tasks. The planner supports adding,
searching, updating, removing, and displaying assignments.

## Time Complexity

| Operation | Time Complexity | Explanation |
|---|---|---|
| Add a task | O(n) | Checks for a duplicate ID before adding the task. |
| Search for a task | O(n) | May examine every task to find the assignment ID. |
| Retrieve a task | O(n) | Searches for the requested assignment ID. |
| Update a task | O(n) | Searches for the task before changing its details. |
| Remove a task | O(n) | Searches for the task and may shift remaining list elements. |
| Display all tasks | O(n) | Visits each task in the list. |
| Count completed tasks | O(n) | Checks every task to count completed assignments. |
| Count all tasks | O(1) | Returns the list's size. |

Here, n represents the number of assignments stored
in the planner.

## Space Complexity

The planner uses O(n) space to store n assignment tasks.
The getAllTasks() method also creates a copy of the list,
which requires O(n) additional space.